# Secrets
.env
.env.*

# Infrastructure
# The sandbox provisions to $XDG_STATE_HOME/canon/sandbox now. This covers a tree
# left by an older checkout or by a CANON_SANDBOX_DIR pointed back inside.
.sandbox/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Web
# The landing page's build output. tokens.css is generated too but stays
# tracked, since nothing else gates web/ for drift.
web/dist/
web/.astro/
web/playwright-report/
web/test-results/
# screenshot.ts's own sweep. web/evidence/ is `440-surface-capture.md`'s own
# per-case evidence output, and this departs from that rule on purpose: the
# PR-triggered capture job already copies the two `home` cases into
# assets/captures/home/ before committing, which is this repository's one
# committed-baseline convention (every other generated frame the page or
# README depends on lives there too, per Question 1 in
# .canon/plans/archive/feature-render-visibility.md), so a second, separately
# named copy under web/evidence/ would give a reviewer the same comparison
# twice rather than a comparison the generic path does not already carry.
web/screenshots/
web/evidence/

# Demos
# `canon demo run` writes four files beside the plan it drove. The plan is
# committed because its timing is hand-tuned and a recompile refuses to
# overwrite it, and the gif is committed because README.md embeds it. The other
# three are what one command writes again on demand, and the webm and mp4
# are the two GitHub will not render anyway.
demos/*.webm
demos/*.mp4
demos/*.png

# Claude
# The root every gitignored session record sits under. One line covers the whole
# tree, which is what the move bought: what is committed stays in .claude/ and
# what is ignored lives here, so a record folder added later needs no entry.
#
# That holds only while nothing tracked ever lands under .canon/. Git does not
# descend into an excluded directory, so a re-inclusion like !.canon/x/ matches
# nothing and there is no way to carve one out. Nothing enforces the rule.
#
# Both entries are checked against the "# Claude" array in
# tooling/claude/manifest.toml by scripts/core/check-ignore-parity.sh.
.canon/
# The one .claude/ record folder that did not move. EnterWorktree creates a
# worktree here and requires its target to sit here, so relocating it breaks the
# harness rather than the toolkit.
.claude/worktrees/
# The scratch rule's fallback spelling, for a project the record move has not
# reached. Ignored for as long as the guard hook accepts it and
# canon migrate records has targets left to migrate off it.
# canon-keep-record-root
.claude/.tmp/
